This software downloads and uses the following third-party data at runtime. None of it is
included in this repository.

- adsb.fi Open Data API (https://adsb.fi). Personal, non-commercial use; attribution required.
- adsb.lol API (https://adsb.lol). Data licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
- FlyItalyADSB API (https://flyitalyadsb.com), only when the user sets an API key. Data licensed
  under CC BY-SA 4.0.
- The OpenSky Network (https://opensky-network.org), only when the user sets API client
  credentials. Used under OpenSky's terms of use (non-commercial).
- Flightradar24 API (https://fr24api.flightradar24.com), only when the user sets their own API
  key (paid subscription). Data provided by Flightradar24 (https://www.flightradar24.com), used
  under its API terms for the subscriber's own use; never stored beyond a short cache, exported
  or redistributed. Request headers and field names follow Flightradar24's official Python SDK
  (https://github.com/Flightradar24/fr24api-sdk-python, MIT); no code is copied from it.
- tar1090-db by wiedehopf (https://github.com/wiedehopf/tar1090-db), derived from the
  Mictronics readsb database. Used for aircraft type/registration and military address ranges.
- plane-alert-db by SDR-Enthusiasts, Ramon F. Kolb (kx1t) and contributors
  (https://github.com/sdr-enthusiasts/plane-alert-db). Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0;
  individual contents under the Database Contents License (DbCL) 1.0.
- VRS standing data by Virtual Radar Server (https://github.com/vradarserver/standing-data). CC0.
- adsb.im route API (https://adsb.im).
- Planespotters.net photo API (https://www.planespotters.net). Photos are shown only in the web UI,
  with the photographer credit and a link, as its terms require.
- OurAirports (https://ourairports.com/data/). Public domain.
- FAA Releasable Aircraft Database (https://registry.faa.gov/). US government work, public
  domain. Street addresses are not imported.
- hexdb.io (https://hexdb.io), per-aircraft lookups for aircraft the other datasets don't know.
  hexdb.io credits its data to PlaneBase/PlanePlotter, Jim Mason, Steve Hibberd and others.
- FAA Aeronautical Data Delivery Service (ADDS), special use airspace
  (https://adds-faa.opendata.arcgis.com/). US government work, public domain. Queried only when
  the user searches for airspace, and cached.
- Map tiles (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).
- USGS Elevation Point Query Service (https://epqs.nationalmap.gov). Public domain.
